# Settings for running an outside Canopy watcher. Read WATCHERS.md first.
# A watcher is three processes from one image (services/Dockerfile), sharing one Postgres that only you use:
#   ROLE=watcher   holds the key, reads feeds and signs. Block 1 below is everything it needs.
#   ROLE=indexer   records the alarms registered on the AlarmBook.   } both take block 2, and hold no key
#   ROLE=detector  records on-chain signals and vault names.         }
# Keep real keys in your host's secret store, not in a file.

# ---- Block 1: watcher.env, for ROLE=watcher ----
ROLE=watcher
# Your own Postgres. Add ?sslmode=require when it is not on the same private network. Docker env files take each line as written, so put no comment after a value.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:CHANGE_ME@watcher-db:5432/postgres
CHAIN_ID=4663
# From deploy/out/4663/deployment.json.
ALARM_BOOK=
# One chain endpoint. At start the watcher reads the AlarmBook to confirm it is the v2 contract, and refuses to start if it is not.
RPC_URL=
# A new key made only for this. It holds no funds and needs no gas. Keep it out of files, chats and issues.
WATCHER_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Labels new posts. For a compatible service, also set the next two lines. Leave them out to call Anthropic directly.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
#CLASSIFIER_MODEL=
# Approved watcher addresses, yours included. Ask in your application for the current list.
# On chain a new watcher only counts 2 days after it is approved, and every approval ends within 365 days (setWatcher(address, until)).
# Signatures are made under the AlarmBook v2 EIP-712 domain (version "2"), so ALARM_BOOK below must be the v2 AlarmBook.
WATCHERS=0xabababababababababababababababababababab,0xcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcd
# API addresses that take your signatures. No trailing slash. The API in web/src/mainnet.json is one.
WATCHER_PEERS=https://api.example.com
# Use the same feeds and vaults as everyone else, from deploy/services.env.example. Different feeds sign different evidence.
FEED_URLS=https://rekt.news/rss/feed.xml,https://cointelegraph.com/rss/tag/hacks,https://status.circle.com/history.rss,https://status.base.org/history.rss
CARD_VAULTS=0xBeEff033F34C046626B8D0A041844C5d1A5409dd,0xBEEff039907422219Fb367e525954DDC092854d9,0xd0dACE70434fF7567b108B5a8c2a36C150C830FE,0x8c258F25fc6fBe3f01ccC828E2C3840A46a4a9A2,0x37788ff0c1d4e45A7FE06BC7e71e0cc00121d0A8
# Report approvals: a protected local JSON file the operator keeps outside the repo, starting as {"version":1,"reports":[]}.
# Unset means the watcher signs no feed attestations. See docs/operational-hardening.md and services/deploy/report-approval.ts.
WATCHER_APPROVAL_FILE=/run/canopy/report-approvals.json
# Hosted quorum submission needs reviewed diversity profiles while this is true (the default). A watcher-only host sends
# no chain transactions and can leave WATCHER_PROFILE_FILE empty.
WATCHER_REQUIRE_DIVERSITY=true
WATCHER_PROFILE_FILE=

# A watcher does not need Telegram, PUBLIC_URL, RPC_URL_BACKUP (it follows RPC_URL), ROUTER, ADAPTER_4626, PLAN_TOKEN or
# PLAN_PAY_ADDRESS. Leave them out: ROLE=watcher fills placeholders that point nowhere.

# ---- Block 2: chain.env, for ROLE=indexer and ROLE=detector (set ROLE on the command line) ----
# These two roles still read the full settings of deploy/services.env.example. Same DATABASE_URL, CHAIN_ID and ALARM_BOOK as above, plus:
# A keyed endpoint from a provider. The backup must be a different provider.
# The same RPC_URL as above.
#RPC_URL=https://rpc.example.com/YOUR_KEY
#RPC_URL_BACKUP=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
# From deploy/out/4663/deployment.json: router, adapter, startBlock, stable (the plan token) and planPayTo.
#ROUTER=
#ADAPTER_4626=
#START_BLOCK=
#PLAN_TOKEN=
#PLAN_PAY_ADDRESS=
# The same CARD_VAULTS list as above.
#CARD_VAULTS=
# Required by the env check. Nobody follows a vault in your database, so no message is ever sent.
#PUBLIC_URL=https://example.invalid
# A throwaway token from BotFather, and any random string of 16 or more characters.
#TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
